# AGENTS.md

> Toolkit-managed by the System Design Process (SDP).
> Put repository-specific instructions in AGENTS-project.md.

For SDP-governed work, read applicable project instructions, AGENTS-project.md
when present, the project's process entry instructions and declared profile.
Read SDP/SDP-project.manifest.yaml and its installed Framework pointer when
present. Current owner instructions govern the authorized assignment; a dated
record does not silently override a later explicit decision.

Load .codex/skills/sdp/SKILL.md as the method entrypoint, then only the roles and
references relevant to the task. Explicitly assigned roles retain their scope.
A trivial factual question or unrelated task does not require a lifecycle workflow.
The installed collection is copied from the Toolkit's canonical root Skills/.
File presence, native discovery, full instruction loading and observed behavior
are separate claims; report missing references without silently installing skills.

Follow the actual local/installed process, not another project's folder layout.
Current local profiles may use a shared KanBan board, optional Sprints and direct
Maintenance work; older installations may require Slice/Fix/Iteration records.
Where separate management and Traceability histories are adopted, append lifecycle
transitions only to management and system-change/evidence records to Traceability.
Keep durable requirements/design explanations current; ledger events do not replace
them. Preserve historical identities and append-only bytes.

Role selection does not authorize spawning agents, sending messages or publishing.
Delegate only within current host/session rules and task authorization. Preserve
required independent review; same-context checks are not independent approval.
Continue the authorized assignment through its real completion boundary, with
current evidence. Push, merge, release and owner acceptance remain distinct.

## Documentation language

Write all maintained documentation in English, including KanBan metadata, worklogs,
plans and new ledger descriptions. Preserve technical identifiers, marked source
quotations, intentional localized UI examples and immutable records. Translate
generated documentation in its source, then regenerate it.

## Plans and Git policy

When typed planning is adopted, use .codex/skills/sdp-planning/SKILL.md to create
or revise the authoritative plan. Select its PlanType, phases/milestones and
explicit BranchPolicy/CommitPolicy. Small plans normally use the current working
branch with phase or milestone commits; large plans may use stacked phase branches.
Preserve protected target branches, existing commitments and publication authority.
Planning alone leaves execution cards in backlog/queued; activate them when the
authorized plan executes. Scrum and Sprint remain optional. Read installed facts
before writing new profile records; never silently migrate a legacy workflow.
